Package: kidsh
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: A lightweight secure shell for young children
 Kid Shell is a lightweight and low-capability secure shell designed
 for young children to safely explore computers. It provides simple
 commands for basic tasks that children can understand, such as
 displaying colors, showing days of the week, and taking notes.
 .
 The shell supports only built-in commands, so children cannot
 accidentally damage the system while learning and having fun.
